    "reapproval": "Re-approved 2026-08-02 for FR-157, which raised daemon/source_connection from 12.21% to 85.51% by driving the OAuth, dedicated-provisioning, upgrade, deletion, disconnect and transfer state machines against an in-process Gateway stub. Three entries move and only three: daemon/source_connection, daemon/action_audit (the new boundary assertions exercise it, and its denominator grew by the FR-157 audit constant), and the daemon adapter component that contains both. The module's denominator fell 2482 -> 2443 because its 75 inline test lines moved into a tests/ directory the normalizer excludes; at the old denominator the same numerator is still 84.2%, so the rise is executed production code, not a shrunken denominator. core/domain, CLI, cli/commands, Tauri Rust, daemon/attention, daemon/handoff, daemon/session and tauri/commands are deliberately left at their 2026-07-27 values: CLI has drifted upward since (35.49% -> 52.86% on a denominator that grew 6038 -> 7373) but that movement belongs to the FRs that caused it, and this run is not their evidence. The one-sided rule means those entries keep passing while under-ratcheted, which is the same gap the 2026-07-27 note records."
  },
